build-protocol/tasks/sql-delivery-reliability/IMPLEMENTATION.md:87:MySQL Entity commit validation previously accepted blank/repeated delivery Event IDs and absent/mismatched current Entity IDs, so malformed input could reach table preparation or leave a state-history prefix. RED: the malformed-input test resolved a blank-ID commit (`evidence/review-mysql-validation-red.log`). GREEN: validation checks current and state-history IDs against the requested Entity, plus missing, blank, and repeated IDs in both diagnostic and delivery Event families before any I/O. The test asserts no prepare or write calls for each malformed case. The existing valid deadlock/replay and partial-prefix cases remain in the affected suites. The touched builder test now uses generated Todo `TaskId`/`Task` state instead of a scalar message pretending to be an Entity; its old missing-ID expectation was updated to the safe validation text.
build-protocol/tasks/sql-delivery-reliability/IMPLEMENTATION.md:91:Final focused V8: **17/17 files, 174/174 tests pass** (`evidence/review-correction-coverage-final.log`), with **22/22 added-line branch records hit** in the two changed runtime files (`evidence/review-correction-branches.md`). The delivery-client suite passed 129/129. Live MySQL-family integration passed **15/15 on MySQL 8.4** and **15/15 on MariaDB 11.4** (`evidence/review-mysql-live-{mysql84,mariadb114}-final.log`). An initial direct Vitest invocation selected no infrastructure tests; the infrastructure config then selected them but the process-substitution shell environment did not set the URLs, producing a skipped run. A subsequent run with explicit task environment parsing exercised the real databases; the first MySQL run exposed only the obsolete error-message expectation, then both final live runs passed. Typecheck, build, touched ESLint, cleanup, TSDoc, and diff-check passed in the `review-correction-*` logs. The frozen correction awaits the reliability/style re-review; the whole-task release profile and real-process matrix remain open.
